<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>66.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <description>Fundraising Quick Start: keeps CampaignMember.Status in sync with the donor's GiftTransaction lifecycle. Fires on Create and Update, entry-gated to fire only when this GT actually matters for CampaignMember state (Insert, CampaignId change, or Status change). Branches:
1. Reparent — CampaignId changed and a prior CampaignId existed: downgrade the OLD campaign's member (guarded — skip if donor still has a Paid GT or Active GC on the old campaign), then continue to the upgrade branch against the new CampaignId.
2. Downgrade — new Status is a refund/cancel state (Canceled, Failed, Fully Refunded, Written-Off): downgrade the current campaign's member (same guard).
3. Upgrade — everything else: flip the donor's CampaignMember on the current campaign to Pledged/Gave (create if missing).
Runtime gate: FQS_Enable_Auto_Members__c must be TRUE, FQS_Hierarchy_Depth__c must be &gt;= 3 (Tactical), and donor must be a Person Account (org donors skipped — CampaignMember requires a Contact). Event campaigns are NOT skipped anymore: the event ladder now carries a Pledged/Gave rung (SortOrder=5) so a gift on an event campaign upgrades the member above Attended.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>FQS Campaign Member Status On Gift Transaction {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>FQS Campaign Member Status On Gift Transaction</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>

    <!-- ================= DECISIONS ================= -->

    <decisions>
        <name>Route_Change_Type</name>
        <label>Route by Change Type</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>First branch: was CampaignId reparented? If yes, handle the OLD campaign's downgrade before falling into the current-campaign path. Order matters — the reparent branch reconverges to the current-campaign path via the connector on Handle_Old_Campaign_Downgrade so the new campaign still gets upgraded.</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Campaign</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - No reparent</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Was_Reparented</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Old_Campaign</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Reparented</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Old_Campaign_Gate</name>
        <label>Old Campaign Gate</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Same gate as the current-campaign branch, applied to the old campaign: automation enabled, Tactical depth, Person Account. Also skips if the donor still has any other Paid GT or Active GC on the old campaign (partial-refund / multi-gift protection).</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Campaign</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Skip old downgrade</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Downgrade_Old</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 AND 2 AND 3 AND 4 AND 5</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Old_Campaign.FQS_Enable_Auto_Members__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Old_Campaign.FQS_Hierarchy_Depth__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>3.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>varOldCampaignActiveGCCount</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Old_Member</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Old campaign eligible</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Old_Member_Exists</name>
        <label>Old Member Exists?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>If the donor had no CampaignMember on the old campaign, there's nothing to downgrade — reconverge to the current-campaign path. If a member exists, revert it to the starting rung.</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Campaign</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - No old member</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Downgrade</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Old_Member.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Choose_Old_Downgrade_Status</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Old member exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Choose_Old_Downgrade_Status</name>
        <label>Choose Old Downgrade Status</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets the fallback ladder rung based on the OLD campaign's category. Event campaigns revert to Registered (SortOrder 2); baseline campaigns revert to Solicited (SortOrder 1).</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Set_Old_Downgrade_To_Solicited</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Baseline ladder</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Event_Ladder_Old</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Old_Campaign.FQS_Campaign_Category__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Events</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Old_Downgrade_To_Registered</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Event ladder</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Current_Campaign_Gate</name>
        <label>Current Campaign Gate</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Master gate for the current-campaign branch. Checkbox TRUE + depth &gt;= 3 + donor is Person Account. If any fail, the whole current-record flow ends.</description>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - End</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Proceed</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 AND 2 AND 3</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Current_Campaign.FQS_Enable_Auto_Members__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Current_Campaign.FQS_Hierarchy_Depth__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>3.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Is_Status_Downgrade</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Current campaign eligible</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Status_Downgrade</name>
        <label>Is Status Downgrade?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Splits into downgrade branch (GT.Status in Canceled/Failed/Fully Refunded/Written-Off) or upgrade branch (everything else, incl. Paid/Pending/Unpaid).</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Member</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Not a downgrade status</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Status_Downgrade</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 OR 2 OR 3 OR 4</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Canceled</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Failed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Fully Refunded</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Written-Off</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Other_Paid_GTs_Current</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Status is refund/cancel</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Current_Downgrade_Guard</name>
        <label>Current Downgrade Guard</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Skips downgrade if the donor still has any OTHER Paid GT (excludes the current record via Id != $Record.Id) or any Active GC on this campaign. Prevents a partial refund from downgrading a whole-campaign member.</description>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Guard blocks downgrade</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Downgrade_Current</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>varCurrentCampaignActiveGCCount</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Current_Member_For_Downgrade</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - No other paid/active</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Current_Member_Downgrade_Exists</name>
        <label>Current Member (Downgrade) Exists?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>If no CampaignMember exists on the current campaign, there's nothing to downgrade — end. Otherwise revert to the starting rung.</description>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - End</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Do_Downgrade</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Current_Member_For_Downgrade.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Choose_Current_Downgrade_Status</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Member exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Choose_Current_Downgrade_Status</name>
        <label>Choose Current Downgrade Status</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets the fallback ladder rung based on the CURRENT campaign's category (Event → Registered, else → Solicited).</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Set_Current_Downgrade_To_Solicited</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Baseline ladder</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Event_Ladder_Current</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Current_Campaign.FQS_Campaign_Category__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Events</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Current_Downgrade_To_Registered</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Event ladder</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Current_Member_Upgrade</name>
        <label>Has Current Member (Upgrade)?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Upgrade branch dispatch. If the donor already has a CampaignMember, flip Status to Pledged/Gave; else create a new one.</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Member_Pledged_Gave</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Create new member</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Update</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Current_Member.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Member_Pledged_Gave</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Update existing member</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>

    <!-- ================= ASSIGNMENTS (COUNT + STATUS SET) ================= -->

    <assignments>
        <name>Count_Old_Campaign_Guards</name>
        <label>Count Old Campaign Guards</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Populates varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTCount and varOldCampaignActiveGCCount from the fetched collections. AssignCount pattern (same as FQS_Campaign_Child_Count_Update).</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>AssignCount</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTs</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varOldCampaignActiveGCCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varOldCampaignActiveGCCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>AssignCount</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varOldCampaignActiveGCs</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Old_Campaign_Gate</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <assignments>
        <name>Count_Current_Campaign_Guards</name>
        <label>Count Current Campaign Guards</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Populates varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTCount (Paid GTs on this campaign that are NOT this record) and varCurrentCampaignActiveGCCount (Active GCs on this campaign for this donor).</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>AssignCount</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTs</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varCurrentCampaignActiveGCCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varCurrentCampaignActiveGCCount</assignToReference>
            <operator>AssignCount</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varCurrentCampaignActiveGCs</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Current_Downgrade_Guard</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Old_Downgrade_To_Solicited</name>
        <label>Set Old Downgrade to Solicited</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets varDowngradeStatus for the old campaign's baseline (non-event) ladder.</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varDowngradeStatus</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Solicited</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Old_Member_Downgrade</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Old_Downgrade_To_Registered</name>
        <label>Set Old Downgrade to Registered</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets varDowngradeStatus for the old campaign's event ladder.</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varDowngradeStatus</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Registered</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Old_Member_Downgrade</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Current_Downgrade_To_Solicited</name>
        <label>Set Current Downgrade to Solicited</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets varDowngradeStatus for the current campaign's baseline (non-event) ladder.</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varDowngradeStatus</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Solicited</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Current_Member_Downgrade</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Current_Downgrade_To_Registered</name>
        <label>Set Current Downgrade to Registered</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Sets varDowngradeStatus for the current campaign's event ladder.</description>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>varDowngradeStatus</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Registered</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Current_Member_Downgrade</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>

    <!-- ================= RECORD LOOKUPS ================= -->

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Donor_Account</name>
        <label>Get Donor Account</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Retrieves the donor Account to determine whether it is a Person Account (has PersonContactId) and to hand the Contact Id to downstream CampaignMember steps.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Route_Change_Type</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.DonorId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Account</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Old_Campaign</name>
        <label>Get Old Campaign</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Fetches the previous parent Campaign so its category/depth/checkbox can gate the old-side downgrade.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Old_Campaign_Other_Paid_GTs</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Campaign</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Old_Campaign_Other_Paid_GTs</name>
        <label>Get Old Campaign Other Paid GTs</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Guard: are there any Paid GTs from this donor on the OLD campaign OTHER than this record? If yes, skip old-side downgrade — donor still has a completed gift there. Ignores this record's own Id so a reparent doesn't self-count.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Old_Campaign_Active_GCs</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>DonorId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.DonorId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Status</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Paid</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>GiftTransaction</object>
        <outputReference>varOldCampaignOtherPaidGTs</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Old_Campaign_Active_GCs</name>
        <label>Get Old Campaign Active GCs</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Guard: any Active GiftCommitment from this donor on the OLD campaign?</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Count_Old_Campaign_Guards</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>DonorId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.DonorId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Status</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Active</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>GiftCommitment</object>
        <outputReference>varOldCampaignActiveGCs</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Old_Member</name>
        <label>Get Old Member</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Fetches the CampaignMember on the OLD campaign for the donor's Contact.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Old_Member_Exists</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record__Prior.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Current_Campaign</name>
        <label>Get Current Campaign</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Fetches the current Campaign for its category, depth, and auto-members checkbox.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Current_Campaign_Gate</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Campaign</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Other_Paid_GTs_Current</name>
        <label>Get Other Paid GTs (Current)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Guard for current-campaign downgrade: any OTHER Paid GT (Id != this record) from this donor on this campaign?</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Campaign_Active_GCs</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>DonorId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.DonorId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Status</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Paid</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>GiftTransaction</object>
        <outputReference>varCurrentCampaignOtherPaidGTs</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Current_Campaign_Active_GCs</name>
        <label>Get Current Campaign Active GCs</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Guard for current-campaign downgrade: any Active GC from this donor on this campaign?</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Count_Current_Campaign_Guards</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>DonorId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.DonorId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Status</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Active</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>GiftCommitment</object>
        <outputReference>varCurrentCampaignActiveGCs</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Current_Member_For_Downgrade</name>
        <label>Get Current Member (For Downgrade)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Fetches the CampaignMember on the current campaign for the donor's Contact — used in the downgrade branch.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Current_Member_Downgrade_Exists</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Current_Member</name>
        <label>Get Current Member (For Upgrade)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Fetches the CampaignMember on the current campaign for the donor's Contact — used in the upgrade branch. Two separate lookups (upgrade vs downgrade) so each branch can null-check independently.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Has_Current_Member_Upgrade</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Current_Member_Retry</name>
        <label>Get Current Member (Retry after Create fault)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Re-fetches the CampaignMember after Create_Member_Pledged_Gave faults. In bulk DML two GTs for the same (donor, campaign) can both miss Get_Current_Member and race into Create — the loser hits the CampaignMember unique constraint. This retry lookup finds the row the winner just committed and hands its Id to Update_Member_Retry so the ladder still lands at Pledged/Gave.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Member_Retry</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>

    <!-- ================= RECORD UPDATES + CREATES ================= -->

    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Old_Member_Downgrade</name>
        <label>Update Old Member (Downgrade)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Reverts the old-campaign CampaignMember to the starting rung (Solicited or Registered depending on campaign category).</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Campaign</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Old_Member.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varDowngradeStatus</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
    </recordUpdates>

    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Current_Member_Downgrade</name>
        <label>Update Current Member (Downgrade)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Reverts the current-campaign CampaignMember to the starting rung.</description>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Current_Member_For_Downgrade.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>varDowngradeStatus</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
    </recordUpdates>

    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Member_Pledged_Gave</name>
        <label>Update Member to Pledged/Gave</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Upgrade branch: flips an existing CampaignMember to Pledged/Gave. Unconditional overwrite is deliberate — a gift is the strongest signal on this ladder.</description>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Current_Member.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pledged/Gave</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
    </recordUpdates>

    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Member_Retry</name>
        <label>Update Member (Retry after Create fault)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Retry-path update: after Create_Member_Pledged_Gave faults (unique-constraint race) and Get_Current_Member_Retry finds the row committed by the winning parallel Create, flip its Status to Pledged/Gave.</description>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Current_Member_Retry.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pledged/Gave</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
    </recordUpdates>

    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Member_Pledged_Gave</name>
        <label>Create Member (Pledged/Gave)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Upgrade branch: creates a new CampaignMember at Pledged/Gave for donors who gave without a prior member record. Fault-guarded because AfterSave flow batching lets two GTs in the same DML for (donor, campaign) each miss the other's Get_Current_Member; the second Create hits CampaignMember's (CampaignId, ContactId) unique constraint. Fault path re-fetches and routes to Update_Member_Pledged_Gave so the ladder still lands at Pledged/Gave.</description>
        <faultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Current_Member_Retry</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.CampaignId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>ContactId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Donor_Account.PersonContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pledged/Gave</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMember</object>
    </recordCreates>

    <!-- ================= START + VARIABLES ================= -->

    <runInMode>DefaultMode</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Donor_Account</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.DonorId})),
    NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.CampaignId})),
    OR(
        ISNEW(),
        ISCHANGED({!$Record.CampaignId}),
        ISCHANGED({!$Record.Status})
    )
)</filterFormula>
        <object>GiftTransaction</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>

